<body>
    <h1>07.01.2026</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p><br></p>
<p>Attendees: Niels B. (chair), Johan N., Nico P., Pierre R., Yan H., Marku=
s N., Stian K., Thomas L., Stein-Roger K., Victoria N., Davy Van D., Gareth=
 Q., Pierre M., Jacob C., Ivan M., Richard V., Benjamin S., Carlos M., Bric=
e B, Paola S.</p>
<p>Meeting Notes</p>
<p>Agenda</p>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"85bbd9d5-b460-4963-9598-7ec2ef899ffe">Welcome</li>
</ul>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"82e2a2fd-8efc-43d4-8d16-9a4341e97f94">Agenda walk-through=
</li>
</ul>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"151781d6-e65d-4d0e-b069-2efd19293b3c">Review of 2025 - Lu=
cid board brainstorm</li>
</ul>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"e7f46626-517a-4210-870c-264a01e70d09">Roadmap for 2026 - =
Lucid board brainstorm</li>
</ul>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"e7b214b1-144d-478d-8607-5506d79e70ad">Promotional activit=
ies</li>
</ul>
<ul>
 <ul>
  <li data-uuid=3D"aee3f70e-7d33-4bc1-87b0-3447c93f60a7">PTS, Geneva, Switz=
erland&nbsp;</li>
 </ul>
</ul>
<ul>
 <ul>
  <li data-uuid=3D"b754e746-2fe0-44eb-bd56-46db2b652cf5">Media Tech Festiva=
l, Odense, Denmark</li>
 </ul>
</ul>
<ul>
 <ul>
  <li data-uuid=3D"dc25129b-5cb4-4a16-ac02-5d59a5d734b1">IBC</li>
 </ul>
</ul>
<ul>
 <ul>
  <li data-uuid=3D"4645a04b-edf2-4191-8284-580cd6800718">??</li>
 </ul>
</ul>
<ul>
 <li data-uuid=3D"25e6afe1-17ad-413f-9c92-58e1e4ad7cd7">Questions and closi=
ng remarks</li>
</ul>
<p><br></p>
<p>Niels B. (chair) welcomed the attendees and introduced the Lucid board t=
ool to review the activities in 2025 and collect the actions for 2026.</p>
<p>The comments collected, during the meeting, are available at (<a href=3D=
"https://lucid.app/lucidspark/3bd119fd-0b46-4156-9879-1e604476de53/edit?vie=
wport_loc=3D-1443%2C-57%2C4587%2C1719%2C0_0&amp;invitationId=3Dinv_f09116b3=
-fe67-4b0e-b2fe-e3617a88885e" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">link=
</a>)</p>
<p><br></p>
<p><strong>Action</strong>: Niels will share the results coming out from lu=
cid boards via email</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>Niels B. (chair =E2=80=93 TV2.DK) listed the next events during which OG=
raf will be promoted. &nbsp;A demo will be showcased by Niels B. during the=
 &nbsp;EBU Production Technology Seminar(<a href=3D"https://tech.ebu.ch/eve=
nts/pts2026" class=3D"external-link" rel=3D"nofollow">https://tech.ebu.ch/e=
vents/pts2026</a>) at the end of January. &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Ryan McK. (BBC)=
 reminded the group about the ongoing preparation of a video explainer to p=
romote OGraf integration for the MediaTech Festival in Odense. Markus N. (Y=
LE) suggested to create a repository to collect OGraf examples used on-air =
and to increase the promotion activities on OGraf. Markus N. pointed the at=
tention to <a href=3D"https://github.com/Eyevinn/ograf-editor" class=3D"ext=
ernal-link" rel=3D"nofollow">https://github.com/Eyevinn/ograf-editor</a> : =
Eyevinn, a finnish company, has developed an editor based on OGraf. Presenc=
e of OGraf at NAB might be also possible thanks to Adobe and LiveOS</p>
<p><strong>Action</strong>: Niels B. and Paola S. (EBU) will have a call wi=
th EBU Comms to understand better how to promote OGraf.</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>Regarding OGraf adoption, TV2.DK will use it during the next general ele=
ction; YLE has included OGraf in their RFPs. Ryan McK. showed a table listi=
ng current supporters &amp; integrators. Victoria N. (Adobe) informed the g=
roup that she is trying to get OGraf integrated in After Effects and togeth=
er with StreamShapers and Volantmedia they are working to improve the proje=
ct website. &nbsp;</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>One of the comments included in the Lucid Chart was about having a dedic=
ated place where discussions around OGraf can take place.</p>
<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>Action</strong>: Niels B. and Paola S. wi=
ll check what solutions are available</p>
<p><br></p>
<p>Johan N. (superfly) informed the group he has started the GDD migration =
and he is continuing the Control API development. He suggested to keep an e=
ye on github issues &amp; pull requests.</p>
<p>Next calls: focus on the server API.</p>
    </div>
